      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Botanical guide",
        "title": "Herbs & Botanicals",
        "lead": "<p>Herbs and botanicals are plant-derived substances, including roots, leaves, berries, bark and mushrooms, that have been cherished for wellbeing across thousands of years. From traditional herbal infusions to modern nutrition, these natural compounds support everyday vital energy, resilience and balance.</p><p>Modern supplementation allows us to standardise active botanical extracts so you receive a consistent level of beneficial phytonutrients in every serving. When combined with care, herbs work harmoniously with your body's natural systems to maintain ongoing wellness.</p>",
        "hero_image": "shopify://shop_images/Velobiotics-Hero-herbs-botanicals.png",
        "groups_title": "How they are grouped",
        "groups_intro": "<p>Explore our main botanical categories tailored to support different aspects of your health and daily routine.</p>",
        "nutrients_title": "Meet each botanical",
        "nutrients_intro": "<p>Discover individual herbs and botanicals, their traditional uses and how they support your overall vitality.</p>",
        "benefits_title": "What they do for you",
        "benefits": "<ul><li><strong>Support natural stress resilience:</strong> Adaptogenic botanicals help maintain physical and mental balance during busy periods.</li><li><strong>Promote everyday digestive comfort:</strong> Traditional digestive herbs support smooth digestion and nutrient absorption.</li><li><strong>Maintain vitality and stamina:</strong> Functional mushrooms and energy-supporting plants promote natural vigour throughout the day.</li><li><strong>Encourage targeted balance:</strong> Specialized botanical extracts support female and male wellbeing through life's changing stages.</li><li><strong>Provide antioxidant nourishment:</strong> Polyphenol-rich plant extracts help shield cells against routine environmental oxidative stress.</li></ul>",
        "sources_title": "Natural sources",
        "sources": "<p>Botanicals have long been enjoyed in simple, traditional forms including brewed herbal teas, dried powders, liquid tinctures and whole culinary ingredients. Spices like ginger and turmeric remain household staples in cooking for both flavour and wellbeing.</p><p>While everyday foods and herbal infusions provide enjoyable dietary diversity, supplement extracts deliver concentrated, standardised amounts of active plant compounds with daily convenience.</p>",
        "why_title": "Why supplement?",
        "why": "<p>Standardised botanical extracts ensure that every batch delivers a consistent, measured level of active plant compounds. Supplements also offer everyday convenience and undergo quality testing to ensure purity and identity.</p><p>Because botanical extracts can be potent, always check with your healthcare professional before starting a new botanical routine, especially if you are taking medication, are pregnant or breastfeeding, or have an underlying medical condition.</p>",
        "syn_title": "Why probiotics make them work better",
        "syn_text": "Many active plant compounds rely on beneficial gut bacteria to convert them into easily absorbed forms, while a healthy gut lining supports efficient nutrient uptake. Velobiotics pairs quality botanical extracts with probiotics protected by a micro-shield that protects each individual bacterium against harsh stomach acid, delivering active cultures directly to your gut.",
        "syn_link": "Learn about shop ingredients",
        "syn_url": "/pages/shop-by-ingredient",
        "faq_title": "Common questions",
        "products_title": "Shop the botanical range",
        "products_intro": "<p>Explore Velobiotics formulas featuring ashwagandha, lion's mane, moringa, sea moss and targeted men's wellness support.</p>",
        "disclaimer": "Supplements support a healthy diet and lifestyle. They do not treat, cure or prevent any disease. Speak to your healthcare professional if you are pregnant, breastfeeding, on medication or have a medical condition."
      }
